  "Number": 8,
  "Question": "If \\(a=\\log_8 225\\) and \\(b=\\log_2 15,\\) then:",
  "Question Type": "text",
  "Choices": {
    "A": "\\(a=\\frac{b}{2}\\)",
    "B": "\\(a=\\frac{2b}{3}\\)",
    "C": "\\(a=b\\)",
    "D": "\\(b=\\frac{a}{2}\\)",
    "E": "\\(a=\\frac{3b}{2}\\)"
  },
  "Choices Type": "text",
  "Correct Answer": "B",
  "Solution": "The useful relationships are \\(8=2^3\\) and \\(225=15^2\\). By the definition of \\(b=\\log_2 15\\), we have \\(2^b=15\\), so squaring gives \\(2^{2b}=225\\). To write this value as a power of \\(8\\), observe that\n\\[\n8^{2b/3}=(2^3)^{2b/3}=2^{2b}=225.\n\\]\nA logarithm gives the exponent needed to produce its argument. Therefore\n\\[\na=\\log_8 225=\\frac{2b}{3}.\n\\]\nThe answer is \\(\\boxed{a=2b/3}\\), choice B.",
